{"kind":"assert","text":"U2, one point for the planner before review. Request 7e9cad2a says a replaced scope \"publishes up to the upgrade act, then stops\". The upgrade act is a Rules entry, and the replaced scope's journal has its own positions, with no common order. So the head stops at the first pass that sees N replaced, after it publishes the scope's journal through its head at that pass. That covers every entry the scope sealed before N ended. An entry sealed in the old scope after that pass is not published. If you want a different stop (for example, a later pass, or a refusal of new entries in a replaced scope), say so; the current head implements the one above.\nTwo more facts for the review:\n(1) Removing the birth-release trust check lets an install whose release is already untrusted pay one proof request before it stops as revoked.\n(2) The end-to-end case rewrites the Rules reply through a proxy; a Rules 16 room with a real upgrade waits for the U4 witness.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}